00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.140
Wait a second.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.720
Was it rushed or did it take too long?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:05.720
Which is it?

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:06.720
Why can't you guys decide?

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.000
Speaker 2: Health and Human Services assistant
secretary.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.340
And of course, he was our testing czar.

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:14.819
So tell us a little bit, sir, about what this
moment means to get full approval, sir?

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:20.440
Speaker 3: Well, this is a very big moment
in operation warp speed history in the history

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.410
of our vaccines, our fight against the pandemic.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:26.160
Prior to this, we had emergency use authorization.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:31.050
What that really meant is that the public
health benefits outweighed the known and potential

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.230
harms.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.620
This says today, as we know the benefits,
we know the harms.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.080
And this vaccine is safe and effective.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.540
And every confidence can be given to that.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.170
Americans should feel very good, even better
than they did yesterday about getting the

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:45.170
vaccine.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.170
What took so long?

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:49.490
Speaker 4: Oh, man.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:53.140
Speaker 1: The critics are worried this was
done too quickly.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.190
It was it was it done too quickly?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.349
No, absolutely not.

00:02:56.349 --> 00:02:58.730
Oh, what took so long to get this approved?

00:02:58.730 --> 00:02:59.730
Come on, guys.

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:00.730
Come on, guys.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.130
So let's listen to a little bit more.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:06.150
Speaker 3: Well, it is a complicated process.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:10.470
And I know there are many, many good professionals,
incredible professionals at the FDA.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.410
I was acting commissioner.

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:16.630
It does take a while because all the data
is looked at in detail.

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:19.020
